{
  "name": "FraudNova lead gate (webhook)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nChecks a new lead with FraudNova before you accept it. A POST to the webhook carries the visitor's email and IP. The workflow checks the email, then the IP, and replies `accepted: true` or `accepted: false` with a reason and both scores. A lead is rejected for a disposable email, a score at or above your threshold, or a proxy, VPN or Tor IP. It helps marketers and developers keep fake leads out of a CRM or ad network.\nLimits: it works with your own site or any tool that lets you set the JSON body and read the reply. A missing `ip` means the decision rests on the email alone. A failed check never rejects a lead.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a **Bearer Auth** credential named `FraudNova API` and paste your key as the token (key at https://fraudnova.com/dashboard/api-keys). New accounts get 25 free credits; each check costs 1 credit.\n2. Open **Settings** and set `risk_threshold` (default 75).\n3. POST `{ \"email\", \"ip\" }` as JSON to the Webhook's production URL.\n\n### Customization\nUse 85 to reject only the worst leads, or 60 for strict offers. To add the phone check, duplicate *Check email*, use the `/check/phone` URL and a `phone` query parameter. Send accepted leads to a CRM or Airtable node after *Respond accepted*.\n\nTemplates and docs: https://github.com/dahleedam/fraudnova-examples/tree/main/examples/n8n",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -940,
        -300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Receive the lead\nThe webhook receives the lead.\nSettings holds the threshold.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Section: Receive the lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -340,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Check with FraudNova\nOne credit per check.\nA failed check counts as not checked.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Section: Check with FraudNova",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        140,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Decide and reply\nBoth outcomes reply, so the caller never hangs.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Section: Decide and reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "fraudnova-lead-gate",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -300,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "fraudnova-lead-gate"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "setting-1",
              "name": "risk_threshold",
              "value": 75,
              "type": "number"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        -60,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "https://fraudnova.com/api/v1/check/email",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpBearerAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "email",
              "value": "={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.email }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "name": "Check email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        180,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpBearerAuth": {
          "name": "FraudNova API"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "https://fraudnova.com/api/v1/check",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpBearerAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "ip",
              "value": "={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.ip }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
      "name": "Check IP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        420,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpBearerAuth": {
          "name": "FraudNova API"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cond-1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('Check email').item.json.success === true && $('Check email').item.json.data.disposable === true }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "cond-2",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('Check email').item.json.success === true && $('Check email').item.json.data.fraud_score >= $('Settings').item.json.risk_threshold }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "cond-3",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('Check IP').item.json.success === true && $('Check IP').item.json.data.fraud_score >= $('Settings').item.json.risk_threshold }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "cond-4",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('Check IP').item.json.success === true && ($('Check IP').item.json.data.proxy === true || $('Check IP').item.json.data.vpn === true || $('Check IP').item.json.data.tor === true) }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "or"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Risky?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { accepted: false, reason: [ ($('Check email').item.json.success === true && $('Check email').item.json.data.disposable === true) ? 'disposable_email' : '', ($('Check email').item.json.success === true && $('Check email').item.json.data.fraud_score >= $('Settings').item.json.risk_threshold) ? 'high_email_score' : '', ($('Check IP').item.json.success === true && $('Check IP').item.json.data.fraud_score >= $('Settings').item.json.risk_threshold) ? 'high_ip_score' : '', ($('Check IP').item.json.success === true && ($('Check IP').item.json.data.proxy === true || $('Check IP').item.json.data.vpn === true || $('Check IP').item.json.data.tor === true)) ? 'proxy_vpn_or_tor' : '' ].filter(r => r).join(', '), scores: { email: ($('Check email').item.json.success === true) ? $('Check email').item.json.data.fraud_score : null, ip: ($('Check IP').item.json.success === true) ? $('Check IP').item.json.data.fraud_score : null } } }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 200
        }
      },
      "name": "Respond rejected",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        920,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { accepted: true, scores: { email: ($('Check email').item.json.success === true) ? $('Check email').item.json.data.fraud_score : null, ip: ($('Check IP').item.json.success === true) ? $('Check IP').item.json.data.fraud_score : null } } }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 200
        }
      },
      "name": "Respond accepted",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        920,
        100
      ]
    }
  ],
